        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Burmese silk pah-soe. Konbaung Dynasty (1752-1885). ca. 1860. Acheik-luntaya patterns in various colours."@en , "Composed of two identical lengths (each W. 58.4 cm.) handstitched along one side (ie. selvage to selvage). The main body of each length is made up of 3 pattern repeats (W.59.6 cm) of acheik (horizontal wave) patterns with checkered end borders in coral, lime, yellow, dark blue, black and white. Luntaya technique of weaving."@en ;
